From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:27:32 +0200
Subject: Treat an endless instantiation as no further definition in
 canDefineFurther

`canDefineFurther` is a speculative step: when adapting a tree to its expected
type fails, the adapter asks whether instantiating more of its type variables
would help, and retries if so. Instantiating one can recurse without end (here
through constraint adjustment, while the first `read[X in Protobuf]` of a unit
resolves a given). Since 3.10's fuel-based recursion limit (#25937), that
surfaces as "Recursion limit exceeded", a hard error, where 3.9 compiled the
same code. The answer such a step should give is that the type cannot be
defined further; the adapter then reports its ordinary failure, if any, and an
implicit search goes on to its other candidates.

Developed with LLM assistance (Claude Code).

Proscala-Patch: definefurther
---
 compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/typer/Inferencing.scala | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/typer/Inferencing.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/typer/Inferencing.scala
index d2c74268145830d487bf28cd99cfac82cd291d72..4eaa15177ad8a9606057944cca18d2a1ceb0b298 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/typer/Inferencing.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/typer/Inferencing.scala
@@ -35,8 +35,13 @@ object Inferencing {
    */
   def canDefineFurther(tp: Type)(using Context): Boolean =
     val prevConstraint = ctx.typerState.constraint
-    isFullyDefined(tp, force = ForceDegree.failBottom)
-    && (ctx.typerState.constraint ne prevConstraint)
+    // A speculative step (it lets the adapter retry after instantiating more type
+    // variables): if instantiating one recurses without end, the answer is that the
+    // type cannot be defined further, not a fatal error.
+    try
+      isFullyDefined(tp, force = ForceDegree.failBottom)
+      && (ctx.typerState.constraint ne prevConstraint)
+    catch case _: RecursionOverflow => false
 
   /** The fully defined type, where all type variables are forced.
    *  Throws an error if type contains wildcards.
